This directory is empty on purpose, and the emptiness is checked rather than
assumed.

`pnpm check-packages` (scripts/check-packages.mjs) prints "0 packages — declared
empty" here, because `nx run-many` cannot tell that state apart from two others
that also exit 0: a package that declares none of the targets CI runs, and a
directory with sources but no manifest, which Nx does not see at all. This file
exists so Git tracks the directory; the script exists so a green build means
something once the first package arrives.

The Nx plugin lands here, in its own pull request.
